==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 6~10 seconds<sup>180f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 4~6 seconds<sup>120f~180f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 4~6 seconds<sup>120f~180f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Mooth]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Lucky Sloth]] spawns as the boss.

==Strategy==
Though intimidating to new players, this level is actually quite easy. The secret is mass meatshielding. Get [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]] and [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Samba Cat]] (or any other meatshield) and flood the stage with them. Then, pair them with strong long ranged units like [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]]. Do not use [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|U.F.O Cat]] in this stage. It is too expensive for what it does and has very low range. [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan]] can soak up some blows from the Lucky Sloth.

Any unit with over 350 range such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] can safely hit the Lucky Sloth. Even units with under 350 range could work if they are strong enough. Just apply 2 meatshields (if one is [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]] or [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall]]) or 3 if you don't have those. [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] can be useful as the level 3 wave lets him reduce peon density while your melee attackers move in.

